&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="marp-and-slides-expand"&gt;Marp and &lt;code&gt;slides expand&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="marp-and-slides-expand"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#marp-and-slides-expand" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Marp reads &lt;code&gt;---hcl&lt;/code&gt; as the start of a front matter too — its front-matter
rule opens on any first line that begins with three dashes — and, the block
not being a YAML mapping, applies none of it: the deck still renders in Marp,
without its directives. A test pins this against Marp Core&amp;rsquo;s own output.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;slides expand&lt;/code&gt; writes the front matter back as YAML, so the expanded deck is
plain Marp and renders as &lt;code&gt;slides&lt;/code&gt; renders the original:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
